::ENG3_U03_L02_GP_Q01::[MLA.ENG3.R.06] Passage: Speech on Public Duty. A citizen does not serve the city only by speaking in the square. The quiet acts matter also: returning a lost tool, keeping a promise, and teaching a child to tell the truth. A city becomes honorable when ordinary duties are performed faithfully. Great laws cannot hold together a people who have forgotten small responsibilities. What is the topic of the speech? {
~Weather in the city.#Weather is not discussed.
=Public duty and citizenship.#Correct. The speech focuses on how citizens serve the city.
~Building materials.#The passage does not focus on construction.
~Travel across the city.#Travel is not discussed.
}

::ENG3_U03_L02_GP_Q02::[MLA.ENG3.R.06] Passage: Speech on Public Duty. A citizen does not serve the city only by speaking in the square. The quiet acts matter also: returning a lost tool, keeping a promise, and teaching a child to tell the truth. A city becomes honorable when ordinary duties are performed faithfully. Great laws cannot hold together a people who have forgotten small responsibilities. What is the central idea? {
~Citizens should speak in the square every day.#The speech says service is not only speaking in the square.
~Laws are never useful.#The speech says laws cannot hold people together without responsibility, not that laws are useless.
=A city depends on citizens faithfully performing ordinary responsibilities.#Correct. This idea is developed across the speech.
~Children should never be taught.#The speech includes teaching truth as a positive duty.
}

::ENG3_U03_L02_GP_Q03::[MLA.ENG3.R.06] Passage: Speech on Public Duty. A citizen does not serve the city only by speaking in the square. The quiet acts matter also: returning a lost tool, keeping a promise, and teaching a child to tell the truth. A city becomes honorable when ordinary duties are performed faithfully. Great laws cannot hold together a people who have forgotten small responsibilities. Which detail supports the central idea? {
~"speaking in the square"#This is mentioned, but the speech says duty is not only this.
~"Great laws"#This is part of the conclusion but not the clearest example.
~"the city"#This is the topic, not supporting evidence by itself.
="returning a lost tool, keeping a promise, and teaching a child to tell the truth"#Correct. These examples show ordinary responsibilities.
}

::ENG3_U03_L02_GP_Q04::[MLA.ENG3.R.06] Passage: Speech on Public Duty. A citizen does not serve the city only by speaking in the square. The quiet acts matter also: returning a lost tool, keeping a promise, and teaching a child to tell the truth. A city becomes honorable when ordinary duties are performed faithfully. Great laws cannot hold together a people who have forgotten small responsibilities. How does the structure develop the central idea? {
=It moves from a contrast about public speaking to examples of quiet duty and then to a conclusion about the city.#Correct. The structure builds the central idea step by step.
~It lists random duties with no conclusion.#The final sentence gives a clear conclusion.
~It begins with a recipe and ends with a travel plan.#No recipe or travel plan appears.
~It hides the main idea in unrelated details.#The details support the central idea.
}

::ENG3_U03_L02_GP_Q05::[MLA.ENG3.R.10] Passage: Speech on Public Duty. A citizen does not serve the city only by speaking in the square. The quiet acts matter also: returning a lost tool, keeping a promise, and teaching a child to tell the truth. A city becomes honorable when ordinary duties are performed faithfully. Great laws cannot hold together a people who have forgotten small responsibilities. Which paraphrase is most accurate? {
~A city is honorable only when citizens make speeches.#This contradicts the speech.
~Small responsibilities do not matter if laws are strong.#This contradicts the final sentence.
~Citizens should avoid helping other people.#This contradicts the examples.
=The speech argues that everyday honest actions help hold a city together.#Correct. This paraphrase captures the central idea accurately.
}
